// The RSA-PSS signing negative-composition probe world: the minimal
// consumer of `rsa-pss-sign`, which the in-guest provider deliberately
// does not export (class D — see rust/guest-provider/README.md). The
// class-D gate (`just conformance-ct::class-d`) builds a dummy component of
// this world and asserts it does NOT compose with the provider.
//
// The signing guest cannot prove this: its composition already fails on
// `ecdsa-sign`. This world imports nothing the provider withholds except
// `rsa-pss-sign` itself, so its composition failure can only come from
// that interface — the provider's `signature` export rebinds the key
// resources and orphans the import (the mechanism is documented on
// `../oaep-probe/wit/world.wit` and in the `class-d` recipe).
//
// The `polymorph:webcrypto` package lives once at the repository root `wit/`,
// pulled in through the `deps/polymorph-webcrypto` symlink.
package conformance:class-d-pss-sign-probe;

world pss-sign-probe {
    @unstable(feature = rsa-sign)
    import polymorph:webcrypto/rsa-pss-sign@0.1.0;
}
